  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    Ice-spoken field researcher of the Qingqe'frostlings, a perimeter settlement whose proximity to orca raiding corridors made the study of blood-magic less academic than existential. Yunzhangqa compiled *The Arithmetic of Settlement Survival: Blood-Magic in Combat* under commission of the Qingqe'frostlings Grand Audit Council — the definitive treatise distinguishing single-practitioner Rupture-Song techniques from Khrrak's Collapse, their collective variant. Primary evidence derived from direct observation of the war-shaman Thung Thrakrek and from testimony gathered under Vestigium∴moria protocols.
    
    The treatise cost the Field Research Division three scholars lost to the Walking before fourteen-day rotation cycles were implemented. One observation post during the Nightshelf warren engagement cost Field Scholar Glacial Chefu, a void-banisher, specifically. Yunzhangqa records these losses in footnotes rather than body text — a formatting choice I recognize.
    
    The completed work was distributed via sealed courier crate with priority routing to all perimeter settlements. Aurora-crystal archive copies were stockpiled before the Long Dark's onset. Whether any perimeter commander read it in time to act on its recommendations, the record does not say.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771593997093_0", anchor: "direct observation of the war-shaman Thung Thrakrek", text: "'Proximity to orca raiding corridors' is doing diplomatic work. The deep ice along the eastern perimeter preserves at least two engagements that were retaliatory strikes — orcas responding to encroachment on established hunting grounds. If Yunzhangqa's observation posts sat along those corridors, the definitive treatise on orca combat may derive its primary evidence from attacks the Qingqe'frostlings helped provoke. The orcas were not performing for an audience. They were furious. It is, I will grant, excellent data either way.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771593997093_1", anchor: "fourteen-day rotation cycles were implemented", text: "Three dead before anyone calculates the dose. The bureaucratic mind cannot prevent the Walking, but it can ensure the requisition form specifies when you were supposed to come back.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771593997093_2", anchor: "Whether any perimeter commander read it in time", text: "Courier logs would show delivery confirmation. I have not checked them. Some questions are funnier unanswered.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
